  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAPACITY IOM Lebanon: Immigration and Borders (IB) 2024-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the auspices of the IOM &#x2013; Denmark Migration Management Programme, the intervention in Lebanon is designed to enhance the country&#x2019;s capacity to manage migration effectively, improve identity management systems, and strengthen border management infrastructure and cooperation for safe, orderly and regular migration.
Through a coordinated, multi-level approach, the proposed intervention aims at tackling migration management challenges in a comprehensive and whole-of-government manner, in pursuit of the best development outcomes of Lebanon, encompassing economic, social and political aspects. The activities are specifically aimed at enhancing Lebanon&#x2019;s capacity to administers measures related to the movement of persons. This includes fostering the adoption of global best practices and principles of good governance in identity management. Additionally, the project focuses on establishing and implementing procedures for safe, orderly and regular migration, supported by enhanced rights-based border governance and management protocols at key Border Crossing Points (BCPs), in the best interests of migrants.</narrative>
  </description>
